#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run the checks a change needs, before it is pushed.

This is the whole check, and this machine is where it runs; AGENTS.md says why
no GitHub Actions workflow runs it for you.

Groups run at once and report each completed group immediately. Groups that
name the same lane share
something a second process would corrupt, so they run one after another, in the
order they are declared here; a lane runs every group in it even after one
fails, because the ones after it have their own verdict to give.

A group that fills the machine (a Go test run, the web suite, end-to-end
browsers) runs each command in one of a few slots every verify run on this
machine shares, so five worktrees verifying at once queue instead of starving
each other's tests. A command that needs the local plane takes the plane first
and a slot second, so a run waiting for the plane never keeps a slot from a run
that could use it.

A group that passed is not run again while everything it is selected by reads
the same: the same files under its patterns, the same submodule commits, the
same tools and the same commands. The record of a pass is kept for the whole
machine, so a fresh clone or a rebase that left a group's files alone reuses
it. A failure is never kept, and --all or --only runs what they name afresh.
"""

